# CODEOWNERS — review required on the files that decide what the AI may do.
# The installer copies this to .github/CODEOWNERS and substitutes the owner from
# contracts/project.yaml. If you are editing it by hand, replace @your-handle-here.
#
# HONEST SCOPE (C10): CODEOWNERS on its own requires NOTHING. It only bites when
# the repo has branch protection with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled
# on the default branch. Without that, this file is a suggestion GitHub renders
# in the PR sidebar. Turn the branch rule on, or do not count this as a control.
#
# Why these paths: they are the ones where a quiet edit changes what the harness
# permits -- which tools may run, which paths are guarded, which model ladder is
# allowed, what the agents are told. A change here should never land unreviewed.

# Governance runtime: policies, guard scripts, schemas, ledger config
/.harness/               @your-handle-here

# Agent + skill definitions: what the fleet is instructed to do
/.claude/                @your-handle-here

# Contracts: tool registry, workflow DAG, agent fleet, approval flow
/contracts/              @your-handle-here

# CI: the workflows that enforce the gates above
/.github/                @your-handle-here

# The projected governance text every assistant reads
CLAUDE.md                @your-handle-here
AGENTS.md                @your-handle-here
